cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this compiler or its accompanying book, please cite the book below."
title: "FRISCcc — A C-Subset Compiler for the FRISC Architecture"
abstract: >-
  FRISCcc is a complete, executable Java compiler for a deterministic subset of
  C, targeting the FRISC educational instruction-set architecture. It implements
  the full pipeline — lexer, LR(1) parser, semantic analysis, typed intermediate
  representation, an optimizing IR-to-IR pass pipeline, FRISC code generation,
  plus an IR tree-walking interpreter and a bytecode virtual machine. It is the
  running example dissected throughout the book listed in the references.
